-- title:
--   Galois invariance of sections read over a coefficient ring
-- statement:
--   Fix a prime $p$ and a natural number $M \neq 0$, a subgroup $H \le (\mathbb{Z}/M)^{\times}$, and assume $p \mid M$, $p^{2} \nmid M$, that every unit of $\mathbb{Z}/M$ mapping to $1$ under `ZMod.unitsMap` for the divisibility $(M/p) \mid M$ lies in $H$, and $M/p \neq 0$. Assume further that the Laurent series `jqModC ℚ` lies in the subfield `qExpFunctionFieldC ℚ ⊤` of $\mathbb{Q}((q))$ generated by ratios of integral $q$-expansions of modular forms of full level, and let $\mathfrak{X}$ be a term of the structure `XHDRModelAtP p M H hpM hj`, which packages a proper, flat, integral, normal model `X p (ΓM M H) hj` over `R p` together with a curve model $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}$ over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ whose function field is identified with `xHFunctionFieldBar M H`, an isomorphism $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ from $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ onto the base change of the model along $R p \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, and the compatibilities recorded in that structure (including Galois equivariance on $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$-points). Let $O$ be a commutative ring with ring maps $\rho_{O} \colon R p \to O$ and $j_{O} \colon O \to \overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ satisfying $j_{O} \circ \rho_{O} =$ `algebraMap (R p) (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)`, and let $U$ be an open of $X_{O} :=$ `XO (ΓM M H) hj ρO`, the pullback of `toBase p (ΓM M H) hj` along `Spec.map ρO`. Write $X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}}$ for the corresponding pullback along `algebraMap (R p) (AlgebraicClosure ℚ)` and $\mathrm{pr}_{J} \colon X_{\overline{\mathbb{Q}}} \to X_{O}$ for the map of pullbacks induced by the identity on the model and by `Spec.map jO`. Assume that the generic point of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.C$ lies in the preimage under $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$ followed by $\mathrm{pr}_{J}$ of the image of $U$ in $X_{O}$, and let $\mathrm{read}$ be the ring homomorphism from $\Gamma(X_{O}, U)$ to `xHFunctionFieldBar M H` obtained by pulling a section back along $\mathrm{pr}_{J}$ and then along $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{eeta}$, taking its germ at the generic point, and transporting along the inverse of $\mathfrak{X}.\mathrm{Meta}.\mathrm{ffEquiv}$. Then for every $\sigma \in \mathrm{Aut}(\overline{\mathbb{Q}}/\mathbb{Q})$ with $\sigma(j_{O}(o)) = j_{O}(o)$ for all $o \in O$, and every $g \in \Gamma(X_{O}, U)$, the semilinear automorphism `arithmeticGalois (xHFunctionField M H) σ`, which acts coefficientwise by $\sigma$ on Laurent series over $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$, fixes $\mathrm{read}(g)$.
--
--   This is the statement that functions on the Deligne–Rapoport type model of $X_H(M)$ which are defined over the coefficient ring $O$ become, when read as elements of the geometric function field $\overline{\mathbb{Q}} \cdot F(\Gamma_H(M)) \subseteq \overline{\mathbb{Q}}((q))$, invariant under the coefficientwise action of every automorphism of $\overline{\mathbb{Q}}$ fixing the image of $O$. It is used in the chart-reading result [`ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_read_chart_mul_eq_and_isUnit_germ_and_smul_eq_and_evalAt_eq_of_chart`](thm.html#ModularCurve.XHDRModelAtP.exists_read_chart_mul_eq_and_isUnit_germ_and_smul_eq_and_evalAt_eq_of_chart), where invariance under inertia of the parameters of an étale chart near the supersingular points is required.
